s to thank Mr. Gruber for his kindness by finding him a finishing touch for his patio. When it comes to bringing it home, however, Paddington finds some surprises."},{"s":4,"e":7,"t":"Trouble in the Bargain Basement","a":"1979-03-20","l":5,"d":"Paddington visits a bargain basement in a shopping store, in order to find something that was very good value. When he tries a demonstration at making pancakes with a frying pan, he accidentally flips the batter all over the audience."},{"s":4,"e":8,"t":"An Outing in the Park","a":"1979-03-27","l":5,"d":"Paddington goes to the local park to see a brass band concert, and he discovers how Schubert hadn't finished his symphony."},{"s":4,"e":9,"t":"Paddington Dines Out","a":"1979-04-03","l":5,"d":"The Browns go out to a posh restaurant to celebrate Paddington's birthday."},{"s":4,"e":10,"t":"Paddington Takes the Stage","a":"1979-04-10","l":5,"d":"Paddington helped the Drama Society with a performance called The Secret Plan , but during the interval, the actor seems to have lost the actual plans."},{"s":4,"e":11,"t":"Paddington in Touch","a":"1979-04-17","l":5,"d":"Paddington goes to a rugby match to see the Peruvian Reserves against the Portabello Wanderers, and Aunt Lucy joins in the match, too."},{"s":4,"e":12,"t":"Comings and Goings at No.32","a":"1979-04-24","l":5,"d":"Paddington's Aunt Lucy comes on visit, but trouble ensues when she goes to Barkridge's to buy Mr. Brown a thank-you present."}]}